        setup: {
          players: 'Players listen to reading cards and race to capture matching picture cards according to karuta rules.',
          deck: '48 cards. Suits by month: January (Pine), February (Plum), March (Cherry)... to December (Paulownia). Each suit has 4 cards of varying value (Bright, Animal, Ribbon, Chaff).',
          equipment: '',
          dealing: "Each player is dealt 8 cards face-down; 8 cards are placed face-up in the 'field' (ba). The rest form the draw pile.",
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: "Form 'Yaku' (point combinations) and outscore your opponent over 6 or 12 rounds.",
          gameplay: "1. **Match**: Play a card from hand to match a card of the same suit in the field. If matched, take both. If no match, discard to the field.\n2. **Draw**: Draw the top card of the deck and match it with the field. Take any matches.\n3. **Forming Yaku**: If your captured cards form a combination (e.g., 3 Ribbons, or 'Ino-Shika-Cho'), you must decide: **Stop** (Score points) or **Koi-Koi** (Continue).",
          keyRules: [
            'Match by month (suit): play a card from hand to capture a same-month card from the table, or discard to table if no match.',
            'After play, draw one from stock; if it matches a table card capture both, else add to table.',
            'On forming a yaku, choose to stop and score or call Koi-Koi to continue; opponent forming yaku first doubles their score and zeros the caller.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Priority one: The **Sake Cup** (Kiku-ni-Sakazuki). It is the most powerful card in the deck as it allows you to form the Moon-Viewing and Flower-Viewing yaku with only two cards.',
          intermediate: "Denial: Watch your opponent's captured pile. If they have two 'Blue Ribbons', your primary goal is to capture the third Blue Ribbon to prevent them from scoring 5 points, even if it doesn't help your own Yaku.",
          advanced: "When to call 'Koi-Koi': Only call it if you have a clear path to adding another 1 or 2 points (e.g., you need one more Ribbon) AND you know your opponent is missing the key cards for their own Yaku.",
          tips: [
            "The Paulownia (December) suit is mostly 'Chaff' (1 pt cards but useful for the 10-chaff yaku). Don't ignore it.",
            'If you have four of the same suit in your hand at the start, it is an automatic 6-point yaku (Teshi).',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
